  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The evidence from pmid-20560986 describes a 20-year-old female with a personal history of pheochromocytoma and a malignant neuroendocrine tumor of the pancreas, along with a family history of early-onset pheochromocytomas. The proband's mother was identified to have a point mutation (X214L) in exon three of the VHL gene. This clinical presentation and family history are consistent with Von Hippel-Lindau Disease (VHL), specifically the predisposition to pheochromocytoma and pancreatic tumors. The variant *214L (c.641G>T) is a germline mutation associated with VHL. The evidence supports the claim that the VHL *214L variant is a predisposing factor for Von Hippel-Lindau Disease, manifesting in phenotypes such as pheochromocytoma and pancreatic endocrine tumors, and is a rare germline variant.",
